  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA-only multiprofile models are strongest, with scvi_n200 + avgpool reaching 0.650 accuracy and transformer nearly matching it, while image-only ResNet50 is weak. The main uncertainty is whether the RNA encoder choice (scvi vs scgpt) materially affects performance under the best-known multiprofile/avgpool setting. config_008 tests scgpt with the same multiprofile + avgpool design as config_005, isolating the RNA encoder effect. This is the best next use of budget because it extends the most promising direction with a single controlled change, can identify a better RNA representation, and avoids prematurely adding multimodal complexity while image evidence remains weak."
